Note: JACK transport sync — Linux pro-audio, opt-in via `use "@jack"`
Note: Single-builtin surface (Phase 40 JACK-01, D-40-05 best-effort):
Note:   jackSync() → JackHandle
Note:
Note: jackSync reads the running JACK server's transport position/tempo and drives
Note:   the active MusicalContext.Tempo (+ bar/beat) when a server is present. The
Note:   transport BPM is applied only when it passes MusicalContext.IsValidTransportTempo
Note:   (T-40-01 — out-of-range tempo, ≤0 OR >1000 BPM, is rejected, not written).
Note:
Note: Charitable absent-server (JACK-01 / T-40-04): with NO JACK server running (or
Note:   libjack.so.0 absent), jackSync is a no-op — it emits a one-shot
Note:   [jack] advisory, leaves Tempo untouched, and returns a dead JackHandle.
Note:   It NEVER throws; non-JACK workflows are completely unaffected.
Note:
Note: Best-effort (D-40-05): JackSharp 0.4.0 was spiked but exposes no transport
Note:   API, so JACK-01 ships via a hand-rolled minimal [DllImport("jack")]
Note:   jack_transport_query (transport state + BPM only). JACK is a SEPARATE
Note:   opt-in module from @midi at fine granularity (D-40-04) so the Linux-only
Note:   libjack native dep is never force-loaded.
Note:
Note: Clock/sync tempo is a play/loop/preview-only input — NEVER reaches
Note:   writeWav/writeMidi (LINK-02 determinism).

module jack

use "@std"

Note: ===== Internal C# Function Declarations =====

Note: Marker builtin called once at module load (last line of this file). Flips
Note: ExecutionContext.JackEnabled = true so jackSync unlocks.
internal proc __enableJackModule ()

Note: ----- JACK transport sync -----
internal proc jackSync ()

Note: ===== Side-effecting init marker =====
Note: Flips ExecutionContext.JackEnabled = true so jackSync above unlocks.
Note: Without this line, calling jackSync raises "requires `use \"@jack\"`".
(__enableJackModule)
